{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-opg-37123-smooth-4-dimensional-schoenflies-probl-94f17183-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-opg-37123-smooth-4-dimensional-schoenflies-probl-94f17183-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-opg-37123-smooth-4-dimensional-schoenflies-probl-94f17183-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-37123-smooth-4-dimensional-schoenflies-probl-94f17183-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-37123"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Problem Let $M$ be a $3$-dimensional smooth submanifold of $S^4$, $M$ diffeomorphic to $S^3$. By the Jordan-Brouwer separation theorem, $M$ separates $S^4$ into the union of two compact connected $4$-manifolds which share $M$ as a common boundary. The Schoenflies problem asks, are these $4$-manifolds diffeomorphic to $D^4$? ie: is $M$ unknotted?"}, "statement_sha256": "977ba9f7dd91bdfdd8854d3d1104bc711f2ca3b80f720fad5df5822fca80bb63"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-37123-smooth-4-dimensional-schoenflies-probl-94f17183-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-37123"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha25